ts.\n*   Confirmed that creating an "Open 4" is a winning move.\n*   Selected I11 as the move.\n\nThe coordinate for the move is **{"col": "I", "row": 11}**.\n\n\n', 'output': 'Evaluation: The current board shows that Black has a strong offensive position. Specifically, Black has three vertically connected stones at I8, I9, and I10. This formation is an "Open 3" (or "Live 3") because the squares immediately above (I7) and below (I11) are empty. White does not have any immediate lethal threats (no 3-in-a-row or 4-in-a-row combinations). Therefore, Black can focus on converting this advantage into a win.\n\nReason: By placing a stone at I11 (or I7), Black extends the vertical line of three stones into a line of four stones (I8, I9, I10, I11). Crucially, this line is unblocked at both ends (I7 and I12 are open). This formation is called an "Open 4" or "Live 4". This is a guaranteed winning move because even if White blocks one end on the next turn, Black can simply play on the other end to complete 5-in-a-row.\n\nAnswer: {"col": "I", "row": 11}'}
